('CULTURE_URETHRAL','Urethral Discharge Culture',array[]::text[],'panel','Clinical Microbiology','panel','{"clinical_category":"microbiology_culture","specimen":"Urethral discharge","method":"Aerobic bacterial culture with organism identification; anaerobic/fungal/fastidious work-up only when specifically requested and validated.","patient_preparation":{"antimicrobials":"Collect before antimicrobial therapy when feasible; record recent antimicrobial use."},"collection_requirements":{"patient_preparation":"Collect urethral specimen according to organism-specific protocol; for gonorrhea use validated culture conditions and/or recommended NAAT as indicated.","collection":"Appropriate swab/transport medium; notify microbiology for suspected fastidious organisms.","container":"Sterile container or validated specimen-specific transport device."},"specimen_requirements":{"specimen":"Urethral discharge","quality":"Record anatomical site, collection method and specimen quality."},"transport_requirements":{"guidance":"Prompt transport; organism-specific temperature/media requirements."},"stability_requirements":{"note":"Specimen- and transport-medium-specific. Follow IDSA/ASM 2024, manufacturer instructions and locally validated SOP; no universal stability interval."},"rejection_criteria":["Wrong swab, delayed transport, or insufficient specimen.","Mislabeled or leaking container"],"reporting_notes":"Report growth/no growth, isolate identification and isolate-specific antimicrobial susceptibility only when indicated and performed by a validated method. A negative culture does not exclude organisms not targeted or not recoverable by the selected method. AST interpretation must be tied to the adopted current CLSI/EUCAST edition.","source_references":[{"id":"IDSA-ASM-2024","title":"Guide to Utilization of the Microbiology Laboratory for Diagnosis of Infectious Diseases: 2024 Update","organization":"IDSA/ASM","year":2024,"doi":"10.1093/cid/ciae104","url":"https://academic.oup.com